1-API:
WHAT IS API?
API stands for Application Programming Interface.
It’s like a messenger between two software systems.
send a request to another and get a response back.
An API lets one application HTTP Status Codes, which tell you the result of an API request.
1xx — Informational

The server received your request and is still processing it.

🔹 100 Continue: Request is okay so far; keep sending.

🔹 101 Switching Protocols: Server is changing protocol (e.g., HTTP → WebSocket).

🟢 2xx — Success

✅ Means your request was successful.

Code	Meaning	Example Use
200 OK	Request succeeded	GET /users worked fine
201 Created	Resource created	POST /users made a new user
202 Accepted	Request accepted but still processing	Background job started
204 No Content	Request succeeded but no data to return	After DELETE /user/1
🟡 3xx — Redirection

↪️ The client must go somewhere else to complete the request.

Code	Meaning	Example Use
301 Moved Permanently	URL changed forever	Page moved to new location
302 Found	Temporary redirect	Login redirects to dashboard
304 Not Modified	No change since last request	Browser can use cached version
🔴 4xx — Client Errors

❌ The request had a problem (your fault).

Code	Meaning	Example Use
400 Bad Request	Invalid input	Wrong data format sent
401 Unauthorized	Not logged in / No valid token	Accessing without login
403 Forbidden	You’re logged in but not allowed	Trying to delete admin data
404 Not Found	Resource doesn’t exist	/users/999 not found
409 Conflict	Request conflicts with current data	Duplicate record
429 Too Many Requests	Rate limit exceeded	Sent too many API calls
🔥 5xx — Server Errors

💥 Problem on the server side, not your fault.

Code	Meaning	Example Use
500 Internal Server Error	Generic server crash	Code bug or failed DB query
502 Bad Gateway	Invalid response from another server	Load balancer issue
503 Service Unavailable	Server down or overloaded	Maintenance mode
504 Gateway Timeout	Server took too long to respond	Timeout in backend service

✅ Summary Tip to Remember:

2xx = Success

3xx = Redirect

4xx = Client Error

5xx = Server Error


