22-RESTART POLICES:
Kubernetes decides what to do if a container fails based on the restartPolicy set in the Pod spec.
There are 3 types:
Policy                 	What it means	                                                              Used in
Always 	Restart the container whenever it stops (even if exit code = 0).	               Default for Deployments, ReplicaSets, DaemonSets
OnFailure	Restart only if the container fails (non-zero exit code).	                              Jobs
Never	        Don’t restart the container, even if it fails.	                                     Jobs, Pods for debugging
      

23-IMAGE PULL POLICY:
ImagePullPolicy tells Kubernetes when to pull (download) the container image from a registry.
🔹 Types of Image Pull Policies
Policy	                               Meaning                                                 When Used
Always	                Always pull the image every time the Pod starts	                     Latest dev builds or CI/CD environments
IfNotPresent	        Pull only if the image is not already on the node                          Stable production images
Never	                Never pull; use only local images	                                     Offline or air-gapped setups


