release name in config file:
You want to use the Helm release name (the name you provide when installing with helm install <release-name> ...) inside your Kubernetes manifests.

🧩 How it works

Helm provides a built-in variable called .Release.Name that stores the release name.

You can use it anywhere in your template files.

📘 Example

values.yaml

app:
  key: "some-value"


configmap.yaml

apiVersion: v1
kind: ConfigMap
metadata:
  name: {{ .Release.Name }}-config
data:
  key: {{ .Values.app.key }}

When you install the chart:

helm install myapp ./mychart


Helm replaces .Release.Name with myapp.

✅ Rendered Output
apiVersion: v1
kind: ConfigMap
metadata:
  name: myapp-config
data:
  key: some-value

🧠 Other useful .Release variables
Variable	Meaning
.Release.Name	Name of the release (given during helm install)
.Release.Namespace	Namespace where Helm is deploying
.Release.Service	The name of the Helm service (usually “Helm”)
.Release.Revision	Revision number of the release
💡 Tip

You can combine it with with blocks too:

{{- with .Values.app }}
metadata:
  name: {{ $.Release.Name }}-{{ .name }}
{{- end }}


Note: use $ to refer to the root context (so you can still access .Release even inside a with block).



Helm provides this through .Chart.Name

You can use the variable .Chart.Name in your templates to refer to the chart name.

📘 Example

Chart.yaml

apiVersion: v2
name: mychart
version: 1.0.0
description: A sample Helm chart


values.yaml

app:
  key: "value123"


configmap.yaml

apiVersion: v1
kind: ConfigMap
metadata:
  name: {{ .Chart.Name }}-config
data:
  key: {{ .Values.app.key }}

🧾 When you install:
helm install testrelease ./mychart

✅ Rendered output:
apiVersion: v1
kind: ConfigMap
metadata:
  name: mychart-config
data:
  key: value123

💡 Common chart-related template variables
Variable	Description
.Chart.Name	The name of the chart (from Chart.yaml)
.Chart.Version	The version of the chart
.Chart.AppVersion	The version of the app (from Chart.yaml)
.Release.Name	The name of the Helm release
.Release.Namespace	The target namespace
🔧 Combined example:

If you want both release name and chart name together (useful for unique resource names):

metadata:
  name: {{ .Release.Name }}-{{ .Chart.Name }}-config


